# Blog posts (Hung Blog)

## Frontmatter (required)

`title`, `description`, `pubDate` (`YYYY-MM-DD`), `category`, `tags` (kebab-case), `lang`, `slug`, `translationKey`.

Optional: `updatedDate`, `series`, `draft`.

- **`lang` matches folder**: `src/content/blog/en/` → `lang: "en"`, `vi/` → `lang: "vi"`.
- **`slug` = filename** (kebab-case). URL: `/{lang}/blog/{slug}/`.
- **`category`** — only values from `src/content.config.ts`: `claude`, `web-development`, `programming`, `devops`, `database`, `system-design`, `notes`.
- Do not edit `content.config.ts` or `src/lib/i18n.ts` unless the user asks to add a category.

## Bilingual (en + vi)

Same `translationKey` on both versions; `slug` may differ per language. Translate `title`, `description`, and body. Localize `series.title`.

```yaml
# en/my-post.md
lang: "en"
slug: "my-post"
translationKey: "my-post"
# vi/bai-cua-toi.md
lang: "vi"
slug: "bai-cua-toi"
translationKey: "my-post"
```

## Series (optional)

```yaml
series:
  id: "series-id"      # same across all parts
  title: "Series Title" # localized per lang
  order: 1             # unique per lang + series.id; match docs/series roadmap
```

## Draft

`draft: true` — excluded from public routes. Remind the user to remove `draft` before publishing.

## Markdown body

- Short intro before the first `##` section.
- Fenced code blocks with a language tag; use `title="path/to/file"` for file paths.
- Mermaid: fenced block with language `mermaid`.
- External `https://` links open in a new tab automatically — do not add `target="_blank"` manually.

## Voice (Hung Blog)

- **vi**: Clear prose; **bold** key terms on first use; avoid overly long paragraphs.
- **en**: Equivalent meaning, not word-for-word translation.
- Technical posts: brief “why” → concepts → runnable demo/commands → “read next” for series.
